From 5b4f3275851e2d5bcb6d1c1de8753da789a4bf5d Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Christopher Owen <3221756+christopherowen@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sun, 8 Nov 2026 13:52:45 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] perf(dsv41): fast-path multi-turn chat rendering and segment
 tokenization
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Eliminate quadratic message scanning, redundant full-conversation deep
copies, unfactored 1,283-branch control-spelling regex backtracking, and
single-threaded full-prompt re-tokenization on deep (100-500+ turn)
DeepSeek-V4.1 coding-agent conversations:

- Compute `last_user_idx = find_last_user_index(full_messages)` once in
  `encode_messages()` and forward it into `_drop_thinking_messages()` and
  `render_message()`, avoiding O(M^2) backward scans across merged tool
  turns; join rendered message chunks in a single pass, replace
  per-message `copy.deepcopy()` in `_normalize_messages()` and
  `merge_tool_messages()` with shallow message/block copies, and skip
  single-item group/block sorting allocations in `order_tool_results()`
  and `sort_tool_results_by_call_order()`.
- Compile `_ControlSpellings` and `template_controls` patterns as
  prefix-factored character tries (`_compile_trie_regex`) instead of
  1,283-branch flat alternations, skip `json.loads()` in `_strings()`
  when tool arguments contain no backslash escapes, check candidate
  private-use sentinels with O(1) UCS-4 membership (`chr(code) in text`),
  and guard `controls.restore()` with `self.open not in text`.
- Split rendered prompts along structural added-token boundaries
  (`<｜end▁of▁sentence｜>`, `<｜User｜>`, `<｜Assistant｜>`) when
  `can_split_segments` holds, caching tokenized turn segments in a
  bounded `_SEGMENT_CACHES` map (`_MAX_SEGMENT_CACHE = 8192`) and
  encoding uncached segments in parallel via
  `backend_tokenizer.encode_batch(..., add_special_tokens=False)` (or
  direct `backend_tokenizer.encode` for small incremental deltas); also
  deduplicate and cache plain-text pieces in `encode_with_text_spellings`.
- Fast-path `content is None` and `isinstance(content, str)` in
  `_parse_chat_message_content()` without allocating a
  `MultiModalContentParser` or `ChatCompletionContentPartTextParam`
  wrapper per text message while preserving reserved prompt-embeds
  placeholder rejection.

Base: 19f2c20ed4d64ae22bd009ceacadd85e2a81e354
Quality: 100% bitwise-identical prompt strings and token ID sequences
across all reference fixtures, multi-turn tool-call benchmarks, and
control-spelling injection locations.
Tests: pytest tests/tokenizers_/test_deepseek_v41.py tests/tokenizers_/test_deepseek_v41_effort.py tests/tokenizers_/test_deepseek_v4.py tests/parser/engine/test_deepseek_v4.py tests/parser/engine/test_deepseek_v41.py tests/entrypoints/openai/test_reasoning_enable_thinking.py tests/entrypoints/openai/test_tool_calls_serialization.py (413 passed across 2 boots)
